<Section
  id="insight"
  label="How it works"
  title="No index to build, store, or repair"
  lede="The engine computes where a record lives from the record itself. There is no catalogue to grow with the data, and no structure to rebuild after a power cut."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Two machines that observe the same thing arrive at the same address without talking to each
      other, so a record can be checked by recomputing its address. The check does not depend on
      trusting the system that wrote it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Time is one of the axes, so a window is a query rather than a reconstruction. The memory an
      answer costs stays flat as the record grows, which is what lets the engine run inside the
      memory a small part carries.
    </p>
  </div>
</Section>
